control.corrective_hint:
Your dialogue is too long.

Previous attempt: 1875 characters (~144s).
Target: 90s.
Hard acceptance ceiling: 1404 characters (~108s).
You must remove at least 471 characters.

Rewrite the SAME scene to approximately 1292 characters (~99s), leaving comfortable headroom below the hard ceiling.

Preserve the conversational beats and causal chain. Do not solve this primarily by deleting turns.

Make the LANGUAGE lighter:
  * prefer short direct replies when natural;
  * fragments are allowed;
  * one idea per turn where possible;
  * short reactions are valuable;
  * remove second or third clauses that merely explain the reaction;
  * remove explanations the previous line already made obvious;
  * remove duplicated setup;
  * remove repeated framing;
  * remove decorative language that does not change the scene;
  * do not narrate why a response is causally connected — let the response itself make that clear.

Preserve: character identity; factual grounding; conversational causality; the scene's arc; the ending payoff.

